---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CodeExample from "../../components/CodeExample.astro";
import PageIntro from "../../components/PageIntro.astro";
import { examples } from "../../lib/examples";

const hello = examples.find((example) => example.id === "hello");
if (hello === undefined) throw new Error("The hello example is required.");
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Lesson 1: Ndewo Ụwa"
  description="Run your first Kwechiri program and understand its output."
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="Tutorial 01"
    title="Ndewo Ụwa"
    lead="Run one complete Kwechiri program and understand how a source file produces output."
    meta="Beginner · No previous programming experience required"
  />

  <div class="shell content-layout">
    <nav class="docs-nav" aria-label="Tutorial navigation">
      <a href="/tutorials/" aria-current="page">Lesson 1: Ndewo Ụwa</a>
      <span>Variables · Planned</span>
      <span>Decisions · Planned</span>
      <span>Loops · Planned</span>
    </nav>
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>Before you begin</h2>
      <p>You need Git, Node.js 20 or newer, npm, and a terminal.</p>
      <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/Jmmadubuike/kwechiri-programming-language.git
cd kwechiri-programming-language
npm ci
npm run build</code></pre>

      <h2>The program</h2>
      <p>Open <code>examples/hello.kwe</code>.</p>
      <CodeExample label="examples/hello.kwe" code={hello.source} output={hello.output} />

      <h2>Run it</h2>
      <pre><code>node dist/cli/index.js examples/hello.kwe</code></pre>
      <p>The output is:</p>
      <pre><code>Ndewo Ụwa!</code></pre>

      <h2>What happened</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The <code>.kwe</code> extension identifies a Kwechiri source file.</li>
        <li><code>bipụta</code> is the language's current output function.</li>
        <li>Text between quotation marks is a string.</li>
        <li>The runtime prints the string and adds a line break.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Capitalization and Igbo characters are part of the string. Replacing
        <code>Ụ</code> with <code>ụ</code> changes the output because Kwechiri
        preserves raw string contents.
      </p>

      <h2>Your turn</h2>
      <p>Create a file named <code>ndewo.kwe</code> containing:</p>
      <pre><code>bipụta("Ndewo Kwechiri!")</code></pre>
      <p>Run it and confirm the output:</p>
      <pre><code>node dist/cli/index.js ndewo.kwe
# Ndewo Kwechiri!</code></pre>

      <div class="callout callout--gold">
        <strong>Common problems</strong>
        Use the <code>.kwe</code> extension, straight quotation marks, and the
        correct path to the source file. The current CLI does not execute
        programs in the browser.
      </div>

      <h2>Next</h2>
      <p>
        Lesson 2 will introduce variables and the current value types. Until it
        is published, explore the <a href="/examples/">verified examples</a> or
        read the <a href="/docs/getting-started/">getting-started guide</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
